  "regressions": [
    "Odd-size allocation placement is aligned; original production helper fails 3/4 checks, patched helper passes all 4",
    "C allocation fragmentation: four rounds of 96 odd-size allocations and realloc preservation on each of ext2/tmpfs fixtures",
    "Optimized Rust calloc(SIZE_MAX,2) returns null and sets child errno=ENOMEM, leaving parent errno=EINVAL; no_builtins fixes reproduced unconditional-panic codegen",
    "Second-handle fsync persists shared dirty pages before writer close; raw mock-device data and inode times verified",
    "Inode mutex excludes writeback between dirty-page and size publication for positional and sequential writes; extension and truncate persist",
    "ctime remains independent of explicit historical mtime; directory size grows after directory timestamp update",
    "cwd and retained directory fd remain usable after rename; cycle, empty, symlink/trailing slash and mount-root failures preserve entries",
    "Renaming an ancestor of a mounted tmpfs preserves cwd, canonical paths and unmount at the new pathname",
    "Existing C/Rust filesystem checks and native std program/proc-macro DSO build, load, expansion and execution all pass"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Rust std allocation/TLS dependency remains; no standalone C CRT or no_std libc yet",
    "Initial errno TLS access may allocate and cannot yet guarantee ENOMEM reporting under exhaustion",
    "RV64 static std/probe cross-build only; no new RV64 filesystem guest run",
    "Full mmap/unlink/namespace concurrency and power-loss durability not established",
    "Kernel suite used limine,network,user-fpu,user-vector,sync-debug features; hypervisor feature excluded for this HVF run"
  ],
